# Secrets — never commit.
#
# The bare `.env` rule matched only that exact name. On 22 September 2026
# three files — .env.bak.2026-09-09-1841 and two .env.bak.golive-* — were
# found STAGED on the production server, having been picked up by a
# `git add -A` there. This repository is public, and those files carry the
# bot tokens and the database password.
#
# So: ignore every variant, then re-admit the one template that is meant to
# be committed and contains no real values.
#
# `.env*` rather than `.env.*` because the README tells you to run
# `nano .env`, and nano leaves .env~ behind — which has no dot after the
# name and would have slipped through.
.env*
!.env.example

# Client-confidential material. Kept locally, deliberately not in a public repo:
# the brief and the returned documents contain bank details, real wallet
# addresses and margins, and are marked "not for distribution".
docs/

# Real seed data — real wallet addresses and live rates.
# db/seed.example.sql is the committed template with synthetic values.
db/seed.sql
db/seed.local.sql

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Backups
*.sql.gz
*.dump
